          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "TL 01 SW 3/79 GREAT GADDESDEN GADDESDEN ROW (North side) North Barn at Whitehouse Farm 30m to N of house GV II Barn.  Circa 1700. Timber frame, on red brick sill (renewed),  dark weatherboarded, with steep old red tile roof. A tall 3-bays barn, facing S; at N side of farmyard. Jowled posts, unjowled mid-bay posts and in middle of end gables, mid-height rail jointed in-line, straight tension braces above rail in gables, heavy straight braces to tie-beams, long straight queen-posts inclined to support single clasped-purlin in each slope of roof. Straight wind-braces to purlins. Listing NGR: TL0489113131"
    }
